  What tells Android Auto this app exists.

  Android Auto reads this descriptor to decide whether an app has anything to show in the car. An
  app without it is invisible there no matter how correct its CarAppService, templates and category
  are - there is no error and nothing appears, which is exactly how it failed here.

  "template" is the declaration for an app built on the Car App Library, as opposed to the older
  media and messaging integrations.
-->
<automotiveApp>
    <uses name="template" />
</automotiveApp>
